From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:32:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: mfd: syscon: Add Apple S8000 i2s-switch
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The A9 i2s-switch (AppleAE2I2SSwitch3 in iOS) is a small block of
routing registers shared by the MCA serializers: each register selects
the clock and data source of one pad, MCA or DSP node. The MCA driver
that owns a route programs it through the syscon.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux 7fbe6da5 (J71t ledger 10.5); his DT used
 the compatible with "syscon" without a binding entry.]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
index 945a168b6..6efc0da0f 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@ properties:
               - apm,xgene-mcb
               - apm,xgene-rb
               - apm,xgene-scu
+              - apple,s8000-i2s-switch
               - atmel,sama5d2-sfrbu
               - atmel,sama5d3-nfc-io
               - atmel,sama5d3-sfrbu
